A message of a channel goes out over passes of the session loop, at most 64 KiB on the wire a pass,
and a part of a large one only once the socket is nearly empty (TCP_NOTSENT_LOWAT):
the loop reads the server between parts, and input does not queue behind megabytes in the socket
The client compresses what it sends on a channel with RDP 4.0 bulk compression once the server takes it,
as the clients of Microsoft do: FreeRDP sent channel data to the server uncompressed

